        "title": "Growth Theory: Harrod-Domar, Solow, Endogenous Growth, Convergence",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Growth theory asks: what determines the long-run growth rate of an economy? The models progress from mechanical capital accumulation (Harrod-Domar, 1940s) through neoclassical steady states (Solow, 1956) to endogenous innovation and knowledge (Romer, 1986–1990). Each model makes different predictions about convergence — whether poor countries will catch up to rich ones."
